<title>UK: Airtours dives as Carnival bid hopes fade.</title>
<headline>Airtours dives as Carnival bid hopes fade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Airtours Plc shares fell 44p to 917-1/2p on Thursday, after its U.S. partner Carnival Corp dashed speculation it may bid for the whole group soon.</p>
<p>Carnival said it had no short-term plans to increase its 29.6 percent stake in the package holiday company in spite of the expiry of a standstill agreement today, said a report in The Financial Times newspaper.</p>
<p>&quot;There was a bit of froth in the Airtours price based on the idea that Carnival might want to buy the 70-odd percent it doesn't already own,&quot; said one market maker.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
